@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch feat/443-item-detail-pages); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:448 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "backlog dashboard: item detail pages from RDF data (#443)" ;
    bl:number 448 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:443 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr448 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:443 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-10T20:01:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-10T20:01:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr448Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #443 asked for an in-dashboard item detail page (issue/PR metadata plus agp:TranscriptSummary reasoning) instead of iriLink always sending users to GitHub, but left routing mechanism and iriLink scope explicitly open. Studied backlog_frontend.html's existing Board/Crates/Provenance/Relevant view pattern before adding a fifth. Built a new #view-item section fetching several small VALUES-parameterized queries (mirroring loadBoard/loadEpics's join shape) for item core metadata, labels, and PR-only touchesFile/touchesCrate/closesIssue/relatesToIssue -- or, for issues, the reverse bl:closesIssue/relatesToIssue join, since that is what a visitor landing on an issue actually wants. Reused loadDecisionsBySummary and renderSummaryBlock verbatim rather than forking them, since #444 will improve both places at once later. Verified every query shape against the live dagalog endpoint (scripts/serve-backlog.sh) for real items (PR #300, issue #263) rather than assuming query correctness, since no headless browser exists in this environment to click through the rendered page." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:448 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr448 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr448RoutingDecision, session:pr448ScopeDecision .

session:pr448RoutingDecision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Chose '#item=<encoded-iri>' hash-fragment routing over adding preventDefault-based click handlers or history.pushState. initNav's existing tab switching never touches location at all, so hashchange is a clean parallel mechanism rather than an extension: plain anchor hrefs work with no JS click interception, browser back/forward and bookmarking work for free, and nav-tab clicks only need one added line (clearing the hash) to avoid a stale item view surviving a reload." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered history.pushState with a client-side router matching initNav more closely, but that needs its own popstate handling and offers no benefit over the hash approach for a single parameterized route; rejected as unnecessary complexity for one new view." .

session:pr448ScopeDecision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Changed iriLink globally to route through the new detail view (dropping target=_blank) rather than adding a separately-named helper used only at a few call sites, because leaving most issue/PR references still pointing straight at GitHub would make the new feature look broken/inconsistent. Split out a githubLink helper (the old iriLink body) for the two places that must keep opening real GitHub tabs: the epics view's 'GitHub: <url>' line, where the visible text is literally the GitHub URL, and the detail page's own footer link, preserving the issue's requested 'escape hatch' to real comments/diff/CI." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered leaving iriLink untouched and adding a new itemDetailLink helper wired up only at new call sites, as the issue body suggested as an option. Rejected because it would leave the Board/Crates/Relevant views inconsistent with the new Provenance-adjacent behavior, and the issue itself judged a global change acceptable as long as the GitHub escape hatch survives." .
